                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Loan Defaulters List - CIBIL&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); width: 94pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;"><br></span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 30.4pt; width:83%;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This database has information provided by Credit Information Bureau of India Limited (CIBIL). It contains list of borrowers which include companies and their directors, who have defaulted in their dues to scheduled commercial banks and financial institutions. Suits have been filed against those, who have defaulted loan to the tune of INR 1 crore &amp; above (US $ 2,29,000+) and those who have willfully defaulted INR 25 lacs and above (US $ 50,000 +). Our database identifies defaulters as recorded in the last four quarters listing published by CIBIL.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) Watch List&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 20.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">The Securities and Exchange Board of India is the regulatory body for governing the capital markets in India. SEBI takes action against non-complaint market intermediaries and corporates whose practices are not in compliances with the Code of Conduct prescribed by SEBI&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) &amp; National Stock Exchange (NSE) Companies Watch list&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 30.4pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This database includes names of the companies, which have been suspended from trading or put in &ldquo;Z&rdquo; category due to violation of clauses of listing agreement with the BSE or NSE. It also includes companies put in &ldquo;Unknown&rdquo; category by NSE, which have vanished and don&rsquo;t have any known whereabouts. The database further includes persons associated with such entities, who have been indicted for an economic default and/or for non-compliance of laws/guidelines and/or who are no longer in the specified activity wherever available.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Department of Company Affairs Vanishing Companies Database&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 30.4pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This database includes names of the companies, which have disappeared, or which have misutilized funds mobilized from investors, and unscrupulous promoters and persons associated with such entities, who have been indicted for an economic default and/or for non-compliance of laws/guidelines and/or who are no longer in the specified activity wherever available. This database is compiled jointly by the Department of Company Affairs, Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) and various stock exchanges, which also suggest appropriate action in terms of Companies Act or SEBI Act.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Indian Prosecuted Companies Database&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 20.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This database includes names of the companies and persons, which/who have defaulted in filing the annual returns and/or have been prosecuted under various sections of Indian Companies Act 1956 by the regional offices of Registrar of companies &ndash; Tamil Nadu, Coimbatore. This database is compiled from the records of the offices of Registrar of Companies of states of Karnataka, Jammu &amp; Kashmir, Kerala&amp; Pondicherry.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Directorship Watch List&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 20.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This proprietary database covers the names of directors and senior employees who have been involved in failed and subsequently de-listed companies, those known to have been involved in the Stock Market Scam of 1992 and other more recent scams and also a detailed list of those who have held senior positions in companies known to have been actively involved in some of the most sensational &lsquo;scams&rsquo; (both political and financial) to hit India over the past decade.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Cross Directorships Database&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 14.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Through a variety of databases, Securitas is able to cross &ndash;check for directorships in companies incorporated in India.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">India specific Media Database Searches&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 14.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Securitas has access to the most comprehensive India specific media database covering over 50 digital media sources including economic and financial publications. Articles naming individuals involved in criminal and civil litigation are searched for.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">India Specific Internet Searches&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 20.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Securitas uses a number of advanced and programmable Internet search tools, which allows it to search through numerous international as well as India-specific search engines on the Internet. This comprehensive search methodology covers both the web as well as newsgroups and ensures complete coverage of the net as is possible.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; background: rgb(204, 204, 204); height: 14.25pt; width: 1001pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">Indian Politically Exposed Persons (PEP) Database&nbsp;</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td style="color: navy; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid; height: 20.25pt; width: 907pt;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">This database gives details of those individuals who perform public functions for a government or administrative body, as well as influential people in religious organizations that have a sphere of influence over political, military or judicial matters. The PEPs list also includes persons who have formerly occupied these positions. The database also contains information on the family members and associates&rsquo; of these PEPs.&nbsp;</span></td>
                            <td style="color: black; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; border: 1px solid;"><span style="font-size: 16px;">No Record Found</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </td>
        </tr>
